{"metadata":{"kernelspec":{"display_name":"Python 3","language":"python","name":"python3"},"language_info":{"name":"python","version":"3.12.13","mimetype":"text/x-python","codemirror_mode":{"name":"ipython","version":3},"pygments_lexer":"ipython3","nbconvert_exporter":"python","file_extension":".py"},"kaggle":{"accelerator":"none","dataSources":[],"isInternetEnabled":false,"language":"python","sourceType":"notebook","isGpuEnabled":false},"title":"Template Method Pattern - EHR Diagnostic Pipelines"},"nbformat_minor":5,"nbformat":4,"cells":[{"id":"331c9217-9433-42c3-b118-f7fe961b1a42","cell_type":"markdown","source":"# Template Method Pattern — Automated Medical Diagnostics (EHR)\n\n**CSE 3206 — Software Engineering Sessional · Lab 3**\nRajshahi University of Engineering & Technology · Department of CSE\n\n---\n\n## The problem\n\nEvery diagnostic service must run the **same four stages in the same order**:\n\n> Generate tabular data → Preprocess → Train model → Evaluate\n\n…but the stages themselves must differ:\n\n| Service | Scaler | Estimator |\n|---|---|---|\n| Diabetes screening | `MinMaxScaler` | `RandomForestClassifier` |\n| Heart-disease screening | `StandardScaler` | `SVC` (RBF kernel) |\n\nWritten as two separate functions, the sequence gets duplicated — so the\nmandated order is encoded **nowhere**, and the copies drift apart. In the\nversion below, one copy scales *before* splitting and leaks test statistics\ninto training; the other scales after. You have to diff them line by line to\nnotice.\n\n```python\ndef run_diabetes_pipeline():\n    X, y = make_classification(...)\n    X = MinMaxScaler().fit_transform(X)        # <-- leakage\n    X_tr, X_te, y_tr, y_te = train_test_split(X, y)\n    ...\n    print(accuracy_score(...))                 # <-- accuracy\n\ndef run_heart_pipeline():\n    X, y = make_classification(...)\n    X_tr, X_te, y_tr, y_te = train_test_split(X, y)\n    scaler = StandardScaler().fit(X_tr)        # <-- correct order\n    ...\n    print(f1_score(...))                       # <-- different metric\n```\n\n## The solution — Template Method\n\n`DiagnosticPipeline.run_pipeline()` is a **concrete** method that fixes the\norder once. Subclasses fill in three abstract primitives and may override one\nhook. They control **what** runs at each step, never **when**.\n\n```\nrun_pipeline()               <-- template method (sealed)\n  |- generate_data()         <-- primitive  (abstract)\n  |- split_data()            <-- shared\n  |- preprocess()            <-- shared, calls create_scaler()\n  |- train_model()           <-- shared, calls create_model()\n  |- evaluate()              <-- shared\n  `- on_pipeline_complete()  <-- hook (optional override)\n```","metadata":{}},{"id":"5d3ab86d-c5d6-4ed6-a892-c41b62cfee34","cell_type":"markdown","source":"## 1. Imports","metadata":{}},{"id":"57383864-4888-4afa-8f07-bc3e9e0d4741","cell_type":"code","source":"from abc import ABC, abstractmethod\nfrom dataclasses import dataclass, field\nfrom typing import Any, Dict, List, Tuple\n\nimport numpy as np\nimport pandas as pd\nimport matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n\nfrom sklearn.datasets import make_classification\nfrom sklearn.ensemble import RandomForestClassifier\nfrom sklearn.metrics import (accuracy_score, f1_score, precision_score,\n                             recall_score, roc_auc_score)\nfrom sklearn.model_selection import train_test_split\nfrom sklearn.preprocessing import MinMaxScaler, StandardScaler\nfrom sklearn.svm import SVC\n\nRANDOM_STATE = 42          # one seed: every run reproduces the same report\n\n\n@dataclass\nclass DiagnosticReport:\n    \"\"\"Structured value the template method returns instead of printing.\"\"\"\n\n    disease: str\n    scaler: str\n    model: str\n    metrics: Dict[str, float] = field(default_factory=dict)\n    note: str = \"\"          # filled in by the subclass hook, if it overrides","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-09-27T11:55:14.952718Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-09-27T11:55:14.953017Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-09-27T11:55:19.685177Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-09-27T11:55:14.95298Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-09-27T11:55:19.684238Z"}},"outputs":[],"execution_count":1},{"id":"6e313710-131b-4868-9bcf-63e2dc4055f8","cell_type":"markdown","source":"## 2. The abstract class — the pattern itself\n\nTwo things to notice while reading it:\n\n1. **`run_pipeline()` is concrete and sealed.** Python has no `final`, so\n   `__init_subclass__` enforces the rule when a subclass is *defined* — an\n   illegal override raises `TypeError` at import, not at run time.\n2. **`preprocess()` is concrete but `create_scaler()` is abstract.** The\n   *procedure* (fit on train, transform both) is fixed; only the *scaler*\n   varies. That is why leakage cannot recur in any subclass.","metadata":{}},{"id":"f4ee1fc0-c1f1-4d1f-a266-2f44576c697e","cell_type":"code","source":"class DiagnosticPipeline(ABC):\n    \"\"\"AbstractClass: decides WHEN each stage runs.\n\n    Subclasses decide WHAT runs at each stage. That split is the whole of\n    Template Method.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, disease: str, feature_names: List[str]) -> None:\n        self.disease = disease\n        self.feature_names = feature_names\n        self.model: Any = None\n\n    def __init_subclass__(cls, **kwargs: Any) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Seal the template method (Python has no `final` keyword).\"\"\"\n        super().__init_subclass__(**kwargs)\n        if \"run_pipeline\" in cls.__dict__:\n            raise TypeError(\n                f\"{cls.__name__} may not override the sealed run_pipeline().\")\n\n    # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n    # THE TEMPLATE METHOD - the single source of truth for stage order\n    # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n    def run_pipeline(self) -> DiagnosticReport:\n        X, y = self.generate_data()                                 # 1 deferred\n        X_train, X_test, y_train, y_test = self.split_data(X, y)    # 2 shared\n        X_train, X_test, scaler = self.preprocess(X_train, X_test)  # 3 shared\n        self.model = self.train_model(X_train, y_train)             # 4 shared\n        metrics = self.evaluate(X_test, y_test)                     # 5 shared\n\n        report = DiagnosticReport(self.disease, type(scaler).__name__,\n                                  type(self.model).__name__, metrics)\n        self.on_pipeline_complete(report)                           # 6 hook\n        return report\n\n    # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n    # PRIMITIVE OPERATIONS - every subclass MUST supply these three\n    # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n    @abstractmethod\n    def generate_data(self) -> Tuple[np.ndarray, np.ndarray]:\n        \"\"\"Return the tabular EHR extract (X, y) for this disease.\"\"\"\n\n    @abstractmethod\n    def create_scaler(self) -> Any:\n        \"\"\"Return an unfitted scaler for this disease.\"\"\"\n\n    @abstractmethod\n    def create_model(self) -> Any:\n        \"\"\"Return an unfitted estimator for this disease.\"\"\"\n\n    # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n    # CONCRETE OPERATIONS - written once, inherited by every subclass\n    # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n    def split_data(self, X: np.ndarray, y: np.ndarray):\n        \"\"\"Stratified hold-out split, identical for every service.\"\"\"\n        return train_test_split(X, y, test_size=0.25, stratify=y,\n                                random_state=RANDOM_STATE)\n\n    def preprocess(self, X_train: np.ndarray, X_test: np.ndarray):\n        \"\"\"Fit the subclass scaler on TRAIN only, then transform both.\n\n        Because this lives in the base class, no subclass can leak test-set\n        statistics into training.\n        \"\"\"\n        scaler = self.create_scaler()\n        return scaler.fit_transform(X_train), scaler.transform(X_test), scaler\n\n    def train_model(self, X_train: np.ndarray, y_train: np.ndarray) -> Any:\n        \"\"\"Instantiate the subclass estimator and fit it.\"\"\"\n        return self.create_model().fit(X_train, y_train)\n\n    def evaluate(self, X_test: np.ndarray, y_test: np.ndarray) -> Dict[str, float]:\n        \"\"\"Same five metrics for every service, so results are comparable.\"\"\"\n        y_pred = self.model.predict(X_test)\n        # Random Forest has predict_proba; an SVC without probability=True\n        # has only decision_function. Handling both keeps evaluate() reusable.\n        score = (self.model.predict_proba(X_test)[:, 1]\n                 if hasattr(self.model, \"predict_proba\")\n                 else self.model.decision_function(X_test))\n        return {\"accuracy\":  accuracy_score(y_test, y_pred),\n                \"precision\": precision_score(y_test, y_pred),\n                \"recall\":    recall_score(y_test, y_pred),\n                \"f1\":        f1_score(y_test, y_pred),\n                \"roc_auc\":   roc_auc_score(y_test, score)}\n\n    # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n    # HOOK - empty by default; subclasses extend without modifying\n    # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n    def on_pipeline_complete(self, report: DiagnosticReport) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Optional epilogue. Base implementation does nothing on purpose.\"\"\"\n\n\nprint(\"Abstract primitives a subclass must supply:\",\n      sorted(DiagnosticPipeline.__abstractmethods__))","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-09-27T11:55:31.969498Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-09-27T11:55:31.969962Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-09-27T11:55:31.984647Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-09-27T11:55:31.969931Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-09-27T11:55:31.983711Z"}},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","text":"Abstract primitives a subclass must supply: ['create_model', 'create_scaler', 'generate_data']\n","output_type":"stream"}],"execution_count":2},{"id":"c53f6bca-11e1-4e65-ad67-301d57cc4e85","cell_type":"markdown","source":"## 3. The two ConcreteClasses\n\nEach is roughly 20 lines: three primitives and one hook override. Neither\ncontains any control flow — they cannot influence the order of anything.","metadata":{}},{"id":"9bf8522a-ca91-4c37-9f7b-241018f9cb55","cell_type":"code","source":"class DiabetesPipeline(DiagnosticPipeline):\n    \"\"\"Trees are scale-insensitive; MinMax keeps the dashboard in [0, 1].\"\"\"\n\n    FEATURES = [\"fasting_glucose\", \"hba1c\", \"bmi\", \"age\",\n                \"insulin\", \"triglycerides\", \"hdl\", \"waist_cm\"]\n\n    def __init__(self) -> None:\n        super().__init__(\"Diabetes\", self.FEATURES)\n\n    def generate_data(self):\n        return make_classification(\n            n_samples=1200, n_features=8, n_informative=5,\n            weights=[0.65, 0.35],      # 35% prevalence in a screened cohort\n            flip_y=0.02, class_sep=1.1, random_state=RANDOM_STATE)\n\n    def create_scaler(self):\n        return MinMaxScaler()\n\n    def create_model(self):\n        return RandomForestClassifier(n_estimators=200, max_depth=10,\n                                      random_state=RANDOM_STATE)\n\n    def on_pipeline_complete(self, report: DiagnosticReport) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Hook override: name the strongest risk driver.\"\"\"\n        top = int(np.argmax(self.model.feature_importances_))\n        report.note = f\"top driver: {self.FEATURES[top]}\"\n\n\nclass HeartDiseasePipeline(DiagnosticPipeline):\n    \"\"\"An RBF kernel measures distances, so standardisation is mandatory.\"\"\"\n\n    FEATURES = [\"resting_bp\", \"cholesterol\", \"max_heart_rate\", \"st_depression\",\n                \"age\", \"chest_pain\", \"exercise_angina\", \"vessels\", \"thal\", \"bmi\"]\n\n    def __init__(self) -> None:\n        super().__init__(\"Heart Disease\", self.FEATURES)\n\n    def generate_data(self):\n        return make_classification(\n            n_samples=900, n_features=10, n_informative=6,\n            n_clusters_per_class=1, weights=[0.55, 0.45],\n            flip_y=0.03, class_sep=0.9, random_state=RANDOM_STATE)\n\n    def create_scaler(self):\n        return StandardScaler()\n\n    def create_model(self):\n        # No probability=True on purpose: this forces evaluate() down its\n        # decision_function branch, proving the shared method is reusable.\n        return SVC(C=2.0, kernel=\"rbf\", random_state=RANDOM_STATE)\n\n    def on_pipeline_complete(self, report: DiagnosticReport) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Hook override: report how compact the decision boundary is.\"\"\"\n        report.note = f\"{int(self.model.n_support_.sum())} support vectors\"","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-09-27T11:55:45.686993Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-09-27T11:55:45.687663Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-09-27T11:55:45.698864Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-09-27T11:55:45.687632Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-09-27T11:55:45.697695Z"}},"outputs":[],"execution_count":4},{"id":"3538277c-be90-40a6-b6da-124ba81b37e5","cell_type":"markdown","source":"## 4. Is the skeleton really sealed?\n\nThis turns the pattern's central claim into an executable test. Defining a\nsubclass that overrides `run_pipeline` must fail **at class-creation time**,\nbefore any object exists.","metadata":{}},{"id":"0992fcd4-8943-4d88-bd4f-788d24f7287e","cell_type":"code","source":"try:\n    class RoguePipeline(DiagnosticPipeline):\n        def generate_data(self): ...\n        def create_scaler(self): ...\n        def create_model(self): ...\n        def run_pipeline(self): ...        # <-- illegal override\nexcept TypeError as exc:\n    print(f\"Seal holds -> {exc}\")\nelse:\n    print(\"WARNING: the skeleton was NOT protected.\")","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-09-27T11:55:52.667021Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-09-27T11:55:52.667919Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-09-27T11:55:52.673881Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-09-27T11:55:52.667884Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-09-27T11:55:52.672931Z"}},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","text":"Seal holds -> RoguePipeline may not override the sealed run_pipeline().\n","output_type":"stream"}],"execution_count":5},{"id":"80c71645-7f8b-4b76-a78e-454385083195","cell_type":"markdown","source":"## 5. Running both services\n\nThe client holds the **abstract** type and calls one identical method on every\nelement. It never asks which scaler or estimator is inside — that is Liskov\nSubstitution doing the work.","metadata":{}},{"id":"e14f6c09-08e3-45e9-aca1-cb3e2e40c9f8","cell_type":"code","source":"pipelines: List[DiagnosticPipeline] = [DiabetesPipeline(),\n                                       HeartDiseasePipeline()]\nreports = [p.run_pipeline() for p in pipelines]\n\nresults = pd.DataFrame(\n    [{\"Estimator\": r.model, \"Scaler\": r.scaler,\n      **{k: round(v, 4) for k, v in r.metrics.items()},\n      \"Hook output\": r.note}\n     for r in reports],\n    index=pd.Index([r.disease for r in reports], name=\"Service\"))\n\nresults","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-09-27T11:56:03.852149Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-09-27T11:56:03.853236Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-09-27T11:56:04.6585Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-09-27T11:56:03.853187Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-09-27T11:56:04.657705Z"}},"outputs":[{"execution_count":6,"output_type":"execute_result","data":{"text/plain":"                            Estimator          Scaler  accuracy  precision  \\\nService                                                                      \nDiabetes       RandomForestClassifier    MinMaxScaler    0.8633     0.8283   \nHeart Disease                     SVC  StandardScaler    0.9289     0.9670   \n\n               recall      f1  roc_auc          Hook output  \nService                                                      \nDiabetes       0.7736  0.8000   0.9364    top driver: hba1c  \nHeart Disease  0.8713  0.9167   0.9640  208 support vectors  ","text/html":"<div>\n<style scoped>\n    .dataframe tbody tr th:only-of-type {\n        vertical-align: middle;\n    }\n\n    .dataframe tbody tr th {\n        vertical-align: top;\n    }\n\n    .dataframe thead th {\n        text-align: right;\n    }\n</style>\n<table border=\"1\" class=\"dataframe\">\n  <thead>\n    <tr style=\"text-align: right;\">\n      <th></th>\n      <th>Estimator</th>\n      <th>Scaler</th>\n      <th>accuracy</th>\n      <th>precision</th>\n      <th>recall</th>\n      <th>f1</th>\n      <th>roc_auc</th>\n      <th>Hook output</th>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <th>Service</th>\n      <th></th>\n      <th></th>\n      <th></th>\n      <th></th>\n      <th></th>\n      <th></th>\n      <th></th>\n      <th></th>\n    </tr>\n  </thead>\n  <tbody>\n    <tr>\n      <th>Diabetes</th>\n      <td>RandomForestClassifier</td>\n      <td>MinMaxScaler</td>\n      <td>0.8633</td>\n      <td>0.8283</td>\n      <td>0.7736</td>\n      <td>0.8000</td>\n      <td>0.9364</td>\n      <td>top driver: hba1c</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <th>Heart Disease</th>\n      <td>SVC</td>\n      <td>StandardScaler</td>\n      <td>0.9289</td>\n      <td>0.9670</td>\n      <td>0.8713</td>\n      <td>0.9167</td>\n      <td>0.9640</td>\n      <td>208 support vectors</td>\n    </tr>\n  </tbody>\n</table>\n</div>"},"metadata":{}}],"execution_count":6},{"id":"7789ee92-7d47-43c7-b294-6b8dc3b5b941","cell_type":"markdown","source":"## 6. The result\n\nBoth rows report the **same five metrics in the same order** — not because the\nsubclasses agreed to, but because `evaluate()` is written once in the base\nclass and neither subclass can reach it.","metadata":{}},{"id":"e03daa0f-9bf1-488e-b274-2a317a6c7ab1","cell_type":"code","source":"# Categorical slots 1-2 of a CVD-validated palette.\nBLUE, ORANGE = \"#2a78d6\", \"#eb6834\"\nINK, INK_SOFT, GRID = \"#1a1a19\", \"#52514e\", \"#e3e3e0\"\n\nkeys = [\"accuracy\", \"precision\", \"recall\", \"f1\", \"roc_auc\"]\nlabels = [\"Accuracy\", \"Precision\", \"Recall\", \"F1\", \"ROC-AUC\"]\n\nfig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(9, 4.2), dpi=110)\nx, width = np.arange(len(keys)), 0.34\n\nfor i, (r, colour) in enumerate(zip(reports, [BLUE, ORANGE])):\n    vals = [r.metrics[k] for k in keys]\n    bars = ax.bar(x + (i - 0.5) * (width + 0.02), vals, width,\n                  label=r.disease, color=colour, zorder=3)\n    for b, v in zip(bars, vals):      # direct labels: identity is never colour alone\n        ax.text(b.get_x() + b.get_width() / 2, v + 0.015, f\"{v:.3f}\",\n                ha=\"center\", va=\"bottom\", fontsize=8, color=INK_SOFT)\n\nfor side in (\"top\", \"right\"):\n    ax.spines[side].set_visible(False)\nfor side in (\"left\", \"bottom\"):\n    ax.spines[side].set_color(GRID)\nax.grid(axis=\"y\", color=GRID, linewidth=0.8, zorder=0)\nax.set_axisbelow(True)\nax.set_xticks(x); ax.set_xticklabels(labels)\nax.set_ylim(0, 1.08)\nax.set_ylabel(\"Score (held-out split)\", fontsize=10, color=INK_SOFT)\nax.tick_params(colors=INK_SOFT, labelsize=9)\nax.set_title(\"One sealed skeleton, two sets of primitives\",\n             fontsize=12, fontweight=\"bold\", color=INK, pad=30)\nax.legend(loc=\"lower center\", bbox_to_anchor=(0.5, 1.005), ncol=2,\n          frameon=False, fontsize=9, handlelength=1.1, columnspacing=2.0)\nplt.tight_layout(); plt.show()","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-09-27T11:56:14.100584Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-09-27T11:56:14.10106Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-09-27T11:56:14.387862Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-09-27T11:56:14.101028Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-09-27T11:56:14.387204Z"}},"outputs":[{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":"<Figure size 990x462 with 1 Axes>","image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}}],"execution_count":7},{"id":"22a50335-9374-40b7-8fe5-ea0ae8da3436","cell_type":"markdown","source":"## 7. Conclusion\n\nTemplate Method turns a procedural **convention** into a structural\n**guarantee**:\n\n- The four mandated stages live in **one** concrete base-class method.\n- That method is **sealed** — `__init_subclass__` rejects any override at\n  import time, and section 4 proves it on every run.\n- Only **three** primitives are abstract, plus **one** optional hook.\n- Leakage is **designed out**: `preprocess()` is written once in the base\n  class, so no subclass can fit a scaler on the full matrix.\n- Both services share every line of splitting, preprocessing, training and\n  evaluation while differing completely in scaler and estimator. Each\n  ConcreteClass is about 20 lines and contains no control flow.\n\n**The trade-off, stated honestly:** a new *pipeline* is cheap (three short\nmethods); a new *stage* in the skeleton is expensive, because it touches the\nbase class and therefore every subclass. Template Method is the right bet when\nthe next change request will say *\"add another variant of this process\"*. If it\nwill say *\"do something new to all the things we already have\"*, you want\n**Visitor** — notebook 2.\n\n> The scores differ between the two services because the two synthetic\n> generators differ, not because SVMs beat forests. The point of the table is\n> that two different pipelines produce **comparable** output at all.","metadata":{}}]}